whats rag?

so your compnay has 500go of document in your server
and you were asked to connect AI assistant to answer questions about these documents

avaialbel solutions:

1- search every file by name, whenever a user asks a question

you would think that you will need to create an algorithm to search for every file by name
when given a question
--> THIS IS wrong
doign this means taht you are gonna scan/parse the documents every time when someone asks a question
--> every time a user searches, the ai has the search for the entire documents

2- summarize the work into chunks for easier search

doing pre-processing work, searching for every file and summarize it into chucnks
to make the search fast
--> this is also wrong
doing this means that you will end up with summaries without accurate contexts

3- combine the both methods into one!

LLM takes input through word embedding
word embdding means words == numbers, this is what llm understands


instead of searching the entire 500go of documents, we essentially store these documents by perserving the semantics which means the meaning of those words into a vector embedidng 
and those embeddings into data base as vectors

this is what RAG is:

RAG lets ai looks up information from your own data before generating an answer!

without RAG ai mainly asks from what it learned during training

wiht RAG:
user question
search relevent information documents
give these documents to ai
ai generates answers
==> RAG is useful for private companies with private data
they utulize ai models taht are already trained, and use it with RAG so the output generates
relevnt information with their own private data!

